Declare a domain shader's patch input implicitly sized on the GLSL target.

legalizePatchParam (source/slang/slang-ir-glsl-legalize.cpp) turns an InputPatch or OutputPatch
parameter into a global varying array sized by the patch: `layout(location = 0) in vec3
patch_tePosition_0[3];` for `const OutputPatch<TeControl, 3> patch` in a domain shader. GLSL 4.50
requires a tessellation evaluation shader's per-vertex inputs to be implicitly sized or sized
gl_MaxPatchVertices, and glslang refuses the declaration: "'[]' : tessellation input array size
must be gl_MaxPatchVertices or implicitly sized". The SPIR-V target's module for the same shader
is valid.

This leaves the array unsized for a domain shader on targets other than SPIR-V, which the GLSL
emitter writes as `[]`. The SPIR-V target, and hull shaders, keep the patch size. A regression
test is added as tools/slang-unit-test/unit-test-glsl-domain-input-unsized.cpp.

Measured on v2026.21: glslangValidator -V --target-env vulkan1.2 -S tese refused the domain
shader's GLSL.
